implementationPlan.description:
TRUTH SWEEP. Edit comment and doc text only; change no behaviour. Every rewritten text must be true under the corrected rules, and none may promise that silence kills a hung seat:
(i) a tick that cannot see the tree (no probe, no pid, a failure or a throw) is neither activity nor silence, so while the probe is blind only the absolute cap can end the seat;
(ii) CPU is evidence, never a threshold, and any growth is activity. Measured on this host, a hung `claude -p` burns 125-547 ms of tree CPU per ~60 s and a working one 219-1219 (human ruling 2026-09-18, task-eca3780d). So a hung seat that still burns CPU is bounded by the cap alone;
(iii) the silence kill fires only after a whole window of OBSERVED ticks with no output, no tool child and no CPU growth at all.

